  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "45460969",
      "title": "2_Difference Between Session And Cache",
      "lectureOrder": 140,
      "videoOrder": 140,
      "sourceHash": "a4bd8c6732b88b24d7faae8d96abd6527cb1b6b487507f4cc585fb455350b6a8",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.07,
          "end": 1.46,
          "en": "Everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.46,
          "end": 6.41,
          "en": "So in this video we'll be discussing about caching and the session the difference between caching and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.41,
          "end": 6.8,
          "en": "session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.8,
          "end": 12.2,
          "en": "Actually, most of the people get confused by these two, that both of them are storing the data for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.2,
          "end": 16.16,
          "en": "the user and retrieving it from there, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.22,
          "end": 18.5,
          "en": "But so what is the difference?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.56,
          "end": 25.16,
          "en": "I can use the session instead of using the caching, because session is also fast, like caching as",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.16,
          "end": 30.56,
          "en": "well, because it also supports the database driver as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.58,
          "end": 35.9,
          "en": "So you have to understand that the purpose of these two are different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.93,
          "end": 38.54,
          "en": "Session mean user session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.6,
          "end": 39.74,
          "en": "That's mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.1,
          "end": 48.2,
          "en": "Uh, a single user can have only one session in a specific browser for a specific domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.23,
          "end": 48.95,
          "en": "Of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.95,
          "end": 53.84,
          "en": "Suppose we have our this, uh, application, which is my Laravel dot test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.84,
          "end": 60.84,
          "en": "So if I create a session in this domain, I mean, from this application, This will be my user session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "for this particular domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "This session will be specifically used for current user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "So if I go to another browser I will be not able to access that session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "So it is user specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "So you have to understand session is user specific but caching is global.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "If you cache something it will be globally implemented because it will be stored somewhere in your local.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 93.50999999999999,
          "en": "Or you can also use it in the DB as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 93.69,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "I mean cached data in the DB, but it will be implemented globally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "That's mean no matter which browser the user is using or from where user is accessing, the data will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "load from the source, but in case of the session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "Session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "Session is more secure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "Session is more secure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 114.78,
          "en": "And it is user specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.78,
          "end": 121.24,
          "en": "So if you store any kind of data in your Firefox browser from this this URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 121.24,
          "end": 122.29,
          "en": "Or you can see this domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.29,
          "end": 129.34,
          "en": "So it will be only accessible from the Firefox browser and from the specific domain only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 129.34,
          "end": 136.66,
          "en": "So if you store anything from our this application and you are thinking that okay, so I have another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 136.66,
          "end": 139.12,
          "en": "application from there, I will get that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 139.15,
          "end": 140.11,
          "en": "Forget about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 140.11,
          "end": 142,
          "en": "That never going to happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 142.32999999999998,
          "end": 148.32999999999998,
          "en": "But in case of caching, caching basically store the data globally so anyone can access and any can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 148.32999999999998,
          "end": 154.42000000000002,
          "en": "Anyone will be able to load the data from the caching, but session are different, so session is more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 154.78,
          "end": 156.82,
          "en": "secure than caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 156.82,
          "end": 165.31,
          "en": "That's why when we work with authentication authorization, this sort of critical task we use session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 165.31,
          "end": 167.44,
          "en": "because session is more secure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 167.68,
          "end": 174.4,
          "en": "Uh, I hope you noticed that when I was talking about logging system, I said multiple times that when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 174.4,
          "end": 180.7,
          "en": "user login, it creates a user session, uh, in the storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 180.7,
          "end": 182.08,
          "en": "So that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 182.11,
          "end": 191.68,
          "en": "When you log in, Laravel creates a logging session in your browser so that if you even, uh, close",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 191.68,
          "end": 197.5,
          "en": "the tab and go again in the, in the, uh, browser, I mean, in the application, you will see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 197.5,
          "end": 206.02,
          "en": "you are still logged in to the application because you have a session for that specific application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 206.02,
          "end": 207.76,
          "en": "that that you have been created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 207.76,
          "end": 210.61,
          "en": "Obviously it will be getting expire after some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 210.61,
          "end": 212.17000000000002,
          "en": "So the cache as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 212.17000000000002,
          "end": 215.47,
          "en": "So caching also have a expired ID as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 215.47,
          "end": 221.11,
          "en": "But you can also define a forever cache which will cache your data forever until you are removing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 221.14,
          "end": 221.71,
          "en": "manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 221.71,
          "end": 229.12,
          "en": "So I hope you got a basic idea of what is the difference between the caching and session straightforwardly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 229.15,
          "end": 235.26,
          "en": "Session is a user specific storage, uh, so it will only work with a single user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 235.29,
          "end": 242.88,
          "en": "Caching is kind of global storage, so if you store in the caching, uh, if you give the ability,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 242.91,
          "end": 247.32,
          "en": "any one user will be able to access that caching without any kind of issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 247.32,
          "end": 251.46,
          "en": "And we use caching for uh, storage, large amount of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 258.51,
          "en": "So the things that is taking time, we can cache those data in our cache memory so that it can load,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 258.72,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "uh, next time more fast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "And you for the user kind of perspective or a user part, it will give a little bit more, uh, responsive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 270.36,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "Or you can say, uh, it will load data more fast and responsibly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 285.06,
          "en": "But session are the different stuff session we used for authentication by storing small amount of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 285.93,
          "en": "if we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 285.96,
          "end": 290.73,
          "en": "In that case we use the session like card when we work with the card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 291.03,
          "end": 293.88,
          "en": "Uh, like you want to add a product into the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 293.88,
          "end": 295.5,
          "en": "In that case, we we use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 295.5,
          "end": 300.78,
          "en": "Most of the time we use the session because it is a user specific action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 301.89,
          "end": 304.05,
          "en": "When I will add some product into the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 307.83,
          "en": "Obviously I will be wanting that when?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 307.83,
          "end": 310.92,
          "en": "When next time I will go inside the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 310.95,
          "end": 313.8,
          "en": "My item will be there in the cart, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 313.83,
          "end": 321.99,
          "en": "But in the cache you cannot do that because if you use the cache as the cart, I mean cart logic, everyone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 321.99,
          "end": 325.44,
          "en": "will be able to see the cart product because it is a global storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 325.44,
          "end": 327.45,
          "en": "Anyways, I hope you got the idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 327.51,
          "end": 329.28,
          "en": "Let's not make this complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 329.31,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "I mean simple topic more complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 332.19,
          "end": 334.44,
          "en": "Okay, so yeah, that's pretty much it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 334.44,
          "end": 338.19,
          "en": "I hope you understand the difference between the caching and the session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 338.22,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "You already know how to work with the session, so it is a side, but when we will work with the caching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 351.15,
          "en": "you will see that they are pretty much identical, but they works differently.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
